<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humayun Shah Bahmani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1458–1461</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humayun">Humayun</a> Shah was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> from 1458 to 1461, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-ud-din-ahmad-shah">Ala-ud-Din Ahmad Shah</a>. He appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-gawan">Mahmud Gawan</a> as a leading minister, but his short reign was remembered for harsh punishment of rebels and rivals, which earned him the name &quot;the Cruel&quot; in later chronicles. He was succeeded by his young son Nizam Shah.</p></div>
